Cavern 2.1 (https://github.com/VoidXH/Cavern, tag 2.1) - CPU optimisations of the E-AC-3 Joint Object
Coding decoder, used by linux-atmos/atmos-decode. Output is bit-identical to unmodified Cavern 2.1.

1. JOC transforms and matrix interpolation run sequentially instead of handing ~16,000 tiny jobs per
   second to the thread pool: the synchronisation cost more CPU than the work.
2. GetMixingMatrices copied the "previous matrix" once per timeslot (24x per frame) with the same result.
3. Objects whose mixing matrix stayed zero long enough to flush the inverse QMF bank's history output
   exact silence, so their transform is skipped (programs often carry permanently unused objects).

